.TH MD-VIEWER 1 "November 2026" "xfce-md-viewer 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
md-viewer \- view Markdown files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B md-viewer
[\fIFILE\fR...]
.br
.B md-viewer
\fB\-\-version\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B md-viewer
is a GTK 4 viewer (not an editor) for Markdown files, made for the Xfce desktop.
Each \fIFILE\fR opens in its own window; if the viewer is already running, the
files open in the running instance. The view reloads automatically when a file
changes on disk.
.PP
Several Markdown flavors are supported (GitHub Flavored, CommonMark, original
Markdown, PHP Markdown Extra, and with
.BR pandoc (1)
installed Pandoc Markdown, MultiMarkdown and R Markdown), along with CSS styles,
math, Mermaid diagrams and a table of contents. Choose them from the
.B View
menu, and set defaults in
.BR "Edit \(-> Preferences" .
Documents cannot run scripts or reach the network.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage message and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/md-viewer/styles/*.css
Your own styles. They appear in View \(-> Style and are picked up live.
.TP
.I /usr/share/xfce-md-viewer/styles/
Built-in styles.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pandoc (1)
.PP
https://github.com/Tecktron/xfce-md-viewer
